1. Definitions

"Lewe Labs", "we" and "us" is the licensor of LeweDesk.

"LeweDesk" or the "Software" means the LeweDesk application (the web pages,
the PHP programs, the database scripts, the installer and the documentation),
in the form in which we deliver it, including updates we deliver to you.

"You" is the person or organisation that installs or uses the Software.

"Installation" means one copy of the Software running on one web server
environment with one database.

"License Key" means the key we issue to you for the Software.

"License Server" means the license service of Lewe Labs (LeweLic,
https://lewelic.lewe.com) that checks License Keys.

"Domain" means the server name of the web server on which an Installation runs
(for example desk.example.com).

"Users" means the people who log in to or visit your Installation.


2. License grant

2.1 Subject to this Agreement and, after the trial period, to a valid License
Key, we grant you a non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable,
revocable right to install and use the Software for your own business or
organisation, including to handle the requests of your own customers and
staff.

2.2 A License Key covers as many Installations as its number of activations
allows. Each Installation is registered with the License Server by its Domain.
The number of activations, the term of the license and any further conditions
are stated in your license confirmation and are shown on the License tab of the
system settings of your Installation.

2.3 You may make copies of the Software for backup and for test and staging
environments of your licensed Installation, as long as you do not use them
productively.

2.4 All rights not expressly granted are reserved.


3. Restrictions

You may not, and may not allow anybody else to:

a) sell, rent, lease, lend, sublicense or otherwise distribute the Software or
   make it available to third parties as a service (for example as a hosted
   helpdesk for several unrelated customers) without our written permission;
b) remove or change copyright, license or other proprietary notices;
c) circumvent, disable or tamper with the license check, the License Key, the
   activation or the restrictions of the limited mode described in section 5,
   or use a License Key that was not issued to you;
d) use one License Key for more Installations than it allows;
e) reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the Software, except to the
   extent that applicable law allows it despite this restriction.

3.1 Source-available, not open source. We deliver the Software in source form
(the PHP programs, the database scripts and the built web pages), so that you
can read it, check what it does and install it easily. This does not make it
open source software. It remains proprietary software, and only this Agreement
gives you rights to it.

3.2 Changes for your own needs. You may change the Software to fit your own
needs, for example its configuration, texts, appearance, language files and
code, as long as you:

a) do not circumvent, disable or tamper with the license check, the License
   Key, the activation or the restrictions of the limited mode (section 3 c),
   and do not unlock a feature or remove a limit that your license does not
   include;
b) use the changed version only in your own licensed Installations, and do not
   distribute it or make it available to third parties (section 3 a);
c) keep the copyright, license and other proprietary notices (section 3 b).

A changed version remains subject to this Agreement. We give no support or
warranty for changes, and an update from us may overwrite them; keeping your
changes compatible with updates is your responsibility.


4. License Key, activation and term

4.1 The License Key is confidential. You are responsible for its safekeeping.
Tell us at once if it was lost or misused; we can block it and issue a new one.

4.2 You enter the License Key on the License tab of the system settings and
click Activate. This registers the Domain of your Installation with the License
Server. You can remove the registration (Deregister), for example before you
move the Installation to another Domain.

4.3 The license runs for the term stated in your license confirmation. If it
has an expiry date, the license ends on that date unless it is renewed.

4.4 We may block a License Key if it is used against this Agreement, if it was
issued by mistake, or if the fees due for it have not been paid.


5. Trial, grace period and limited mode

5.1 Trial. Without a License Key the Software runs for 14 days from its first
start, with its full functionality.

5.2 Grace period. If the license is missing, invalid, not registered for the
Domain, not yet activated or expired, the Software keeps its full functionality
for another 14 days. Administrators of the Installation are shown a warning
that names the reason and the days left. A blocked License Key has no grace
period.

5.3 Limited mode. When the trial or the grace period is over, or the License
Key is blocked, the Software runs in a limited mode until a valid license is
activated:

a) no more than 50 issues and 20 users (not counting the built-in
   administrator account) can be created; existing issues and users can still
   be edited and deleted;
b) self-registration, the set-up of two factor authentication, the Audit Log
   (viewing) and the Custom Views are switched off.

Your data is not deleted or changed in the limited mode; the Audit Log is still
written. As soon as a valid license is activated, all limits are lifted.

5.4 The operator of an Installation may choose, in the configuration file, to
lock the Software instead, so that after the grace period only administrators
can log in.


6. License check and data sent to the License Server

6.1 To check the license, the Installation contacts the License Server over an
encrypted connection when the License Key is saved, when you click Activate,
Deregister or Check Now, and automatically about every 30 minutes (every five
minutes after a failed check).

6.2 Only these data are sent: the License Key, the Domain and the name of the
product. The License Server also sees the technical data of every web request
(the IP address of your web server and the time). No data of your Users, issues
or comments are sent. The License Server keeps the License Key, the Domain, the
time of activation and of the last check, and the status of the license.

6.3 If the License Server cannot be reached, the Software keeps working with
the last known state of the license.

6.4 Your Installation's privacy policy (Help > Privacy Policy) describes this
data transfer for your Users. You are responsible for the privacy policy of
your Installation.


7. Your data

You remain the owner of all data you and your Users enter into the Software.
We do not have access to your Installation or your database. You alone are
responsible for the lawful processing of the personal data of your Users,
including their information and, where required, their consent, and for
backups of your data.


8. Updates and support

We may offer updates and support as described in your license confirmation or
on our website. Without such a commitment there is no claim to updates or
support. Updates are subject to this Agreement.


9. Ownership

The Software is protected by copyright. We and our licensors own all rights in
